@startuml sequence-table-review-measured
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: every table region now says what the Ollama review did (outcome) and how much of its markdown is found in the PDF text inside its box (grounded share), so the review can be measured.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram. Scope: one table region inside one tables job of text-tables; the run lifecycle (LeafJob.run) is left out.
' Source: evilflowers-text-service src/evilflowers_text/extraction/tables.py, table_review.py, metrics.py; Text-Service, Decision-Models notes; issue #19 (2026-11-16)
' =============================================================================

title Table review, measured: text-tables, one table region (live once deployed, 2026-11-16)

participant "TablesJob\n(text-tables)" as job
participant "TableReader" as reader <<focus>>
participant "pdfplumber" as plumber
participant "TableReviewer" as reviewer
participant "ollama\n(shared)" as ollama
participant "OTel metrics\n(Mimir)" as mimir
participant "catalog\n/extraction/v1" as catalog

job -> reader : read(path, output_dir, regions)
reader -> plumber : table_area(page, bbox)
reader -> plumber : read_table(area)
plumber --> reader : Grid(markdown, strategy,\nfilled_share, fragment_share, rotated_share)
alt table review enabled
  reader -> reviewer : review(crop, draft)
  reviewer -> ollama : HTTP POST OLLAMA_ENDPOINT (chat, format json)
  alt answer parsed
    ollama --> reviewer : JSON
    reviewer --> reader : Review(markdown, kept | rewritten | transcribed | unusable)
  else HTTP error, timeout, body not JSON
    reviewer --> reader : Review(draft, failed)\nlog "Table review failed"
  end
  reader -> mimir : text_table_review_total{outcome} +1
end
reader -> plumber : area.extract_text()
reader -[$accent_msg()]> reader : <b>grounded_share(markdown, text)</b>\nnumbers whole, words across line breaks;\nnull for rotated text or no text layer
reader -> mimir : text_tables_regions_total{markdown} +1
reader -> reader : log "Table read" (run_id bound by the job)
reader --> job : Region(markdown, provenance =\n{review_outcome, grounded_share, grid_*})
job -> catalog : HTTP POST /runs/{id}/regions\n(per-region provenance)

caption Outcome and grounded share travel in each region's provenance today; EvilFlowersCatalog#189 promotes them to columns.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-text-service · docs/diagrams/sequence-table-review-measured.puml
@enduml
